  <div class="prose">
    <h2>The campground as an energy centre</h2>
    <p>In Saint-Fortunat, the Donjon invents the "energy campground": "The concept is simple… but requires all your attention, and your participation! The idea came from the lodges in the indoor camping hall, formerly meant to house pigs; these lodges form open or closed compartments, excellent during events. Of the eleven lodges, seven were dedicated to the seven energy centres, the seven chakras. The choice and arrangement of each of the chosen elements form a universe conducive to an intimate encounter with each of your chakras. Thus, a healing power emerges."</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>The red lodge</strong>, the earth's, is the Donjon's information booth.</li>
      <li><strong>The orange lodge</strong>, the water's, "all comfort, hushed and intimate", four people.</li>
      <li><strong>The yellow lodge</strong>, the fire's, is reserved for the wood stove: "it heats the place".</li>
      <li><strong>The green lodge</strong>, the air's and the heart's, open and airy.</li>
      <li><strong>The blue lodge</strong>, the ether's and the throat's, enclosed, five people.</li>
      <li><strong>The indigo lodge</strong>, the light's, "a collection of information".</li>
      <li><strong>The violet lodge</strong>, the illumination's, "ready to receive a council".</li>
    </ul>
    <p>"The only condition being to take part in the energy created: bring with you materials and scents linked to the chosen chakra. There is always room to expand the energy network too…" The lodges were reserved for $50 or $60 for the whole duration of an event. Next door, the Art Gallery, a "multidisciplinary hall", with sound and lighting systems permanently installed, where "decorators, hosts, musicians and dancers can at any time give themselves over wholeheartedly to the production of their art".</p>

    <h2>Three founding events</h2>
    <p><strong>New Year's Eve Party 2011</strong>, from December 31 to January 2: "An invitation to come and celebrate the new year on the land in Saint-Fortunat, in the Donjon, at the top of the mountain, where we can host for the whole weekend about 125 people, very comfortably, with sleeping indoors on one side, and on the other a big dance hall, and more people if some like to stay in a tipi or winter camping… There will be a big bonfire, a community kitchen to cook together." $30 at the door, "this money will go specifically to paying the artists, ensuring excellent sound throughout the place, and renting chemical toilets for everyone's comfort". And the final piece of advice: "Don't forget your essentials for a comfortable weekend… especially your slippers!"</p>
    <p><strong>Main d'œuvre ! Dans l'bois !</strong> (Labour! Into the woods!), from February 5, 2011, "in the woods, on the water's edge", the winter worksite.</p>
    <p><strong>Sundari Festival 2011</strong>, June 3, 4 and 5, "a celebration of universal love" with the Dreamtree Project, "the Indian dub fusion project of Juno nominee Adham Shaikh and Uwe Neumann": "Beyond notions of east meets west, Dreamtree conjures a fertile space for all who long to be seduced by the ritual power of music… hold on tight to the magic carpet!" Booths, workshops, activities in nature, and a caravan between Montreal and Saint-Fortunat. "For universal love… which will allow real change."</p>
  </div>

